  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses exclusively on the probability of the maximum outcome and would favor Lottery B (34% > 33%). However, the individual’s reasoning evaluates a trade-off between the magnitude of the prize and the probability, indicating a compensatory process (weighing gains in probability against losses in payoff). The individual does not highlight or prioritize the probability of the maximum outcome as a deciding factor; instead, they reject the small probability gain because it comes at a monetary cost. There is no indication that the individual identified or used the probability of the maximum outcome as a standalone criterion. Therefore, the reasoning process described does not align with the specified decision reason, which ignores outcome levels and focuses only on probabilities of maximum outcomes.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
